  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This recipe makes 6 dorayaki and takes about 30 minutes. Each one is two small, honey-flavoured pancakes with"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "anko"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "red bean paste in the middle."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Cook the pancakes on a very low heat. The batter has honey and sugar in it, which makes it colour quickly at higher temperatures. You want an even golden-brown disc with no dark spots. Let small bubbles form across the surface before flipping."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "ingredientsList",
        "attrs": {
          "defaultServings": 4,
          "items": [
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "eggs",
              "amount": 2,
              "unit": null,
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "caster-sugar",
              "amount": 80,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "honey",
              "amount": 2,
              "unit": "tbsp",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "mirin",
              "amount": 1,
              "unit": "tbsp",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "plain-flour",
              "amount": 120,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": "sifted",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "baking-powder",
              "amount": 1,
              "unit": "tsp",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "red-bean-paste",
              "amount": 300,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": "anko, shop-bought or homemade",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "vegetable-oil",
              "amount": 1,
              "unit": "tsp",
              "prepNote": "for the pan",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Whisk together the eggs and caster sugar in a bowl until pale and slightly thickened. Add the honey and mirin and whisk again."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Sift in the flour and baking powder. Stir gently until a smooth batter forms. The"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "mirin"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "gives the pancakes a slight sheen. Leave the batter to rest for 5 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat a non-stick frying pan over a low heat. Brush with a very thin layer of oil. Use a piece of kitchen paper to spread and remove excess."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Pour 2 tablespoons of batter per pancake into the pan. Cook for about 2 minutes until bubbles form across the surface. Flip and cook for 1 minute more. You should have 12 small pancakes in total."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Transfer the pancakes to a wire rack. Leave to cool slightly. They should be golden on one side and pale on the other."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Spread a heaped tablespoon of"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "anko"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "onto the pale side of one pancake. Sandwich with a second pancake, golden side out. Repeat to make 6"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "dorayaki"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "attrs": {
          "items": [
            {
              "symptom": "Pancakes are burning before they are cooked through",
              "cause": "The heat is too high. The honey and sugar in the batter colour fast.",
              "fix": "Lower the heat and give each pancake a full 2 minutes before flipping. Keep the heat on low throughout."
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Batter is too thick to spread into rounds",
              "cause": "The flour absorbed too much moisture or the batter was not rested.",
              "fix": "Stir in water, 1 teaspoon at a time, until the batter flows slowly from a spoon. Rest for 5 minutes before cooking."
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Dorayaki filling is leaking out",
              "cause": "Too much anko was spread on or the pancakes are too thin.",
              "fix": "Use a heaped tablespoon only. Leave a small border around the edge when spreading the filling."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Dorayaki are a well-loved Japanese sweet associated with the manga character Doraemon, who is rarely seen without one. The name comes from dora, the Japanese word for gong, which the round shape resembles. They are sold in confectionery shops and convenience stores across Japan. At home they are a popular after-school treat and appear in lunch boxes as a small dessert."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}